  concept: "Authored objective: LED 2 On.\nAuthored requirement: Register\n current
    \u2265 6 mA. current \u2264 15 mA. Connection pair LED2_Anode and LED2_Cathode.
    Conduction required.\nGeneral teaching principle: An LED has a defined anode
    and cathode; correct polarity and suitable current control matter for normal
    forward operation.\nOnly fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish that
    this objective is complete."
  analogy: A directional gate with a current limit is a useful model, although an
    LED is not an ideal one-way switch.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: A lit LED alone does not establish that its current and power are
    within safe ratings.
